    private val name = topic(NAME, 42L, "field-initial")
    override fun body(): View = Text(name)
}
```
But the root view is constructed in `app.newRoot()` inside the constructor after context is pushed; eager resolution works. To test the deferred path, we'd need a root constructed before the context (e.g., a pre-constructed view passed to the app), but `PathlandSession` calls `app.newRoot()` inside the context. We can test `Signals.topic` outside context and then read inside a session? Hard. The deferred test covers the failure outside. Field initializer works because of the context push. Add a small test `fieldDeclaredSubscriptionsWork` to ensure the root's field initializer resolves. This also validates the important DX.

